hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1422","Zaid bin Akhram Al-Tai and Ibrahim bin Marzuq narrated to us, saying: Wahb bin Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, saying: I heard Al-Nu’man bin Rashid narrates, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out one day He was asking for water, so he led us in two rak'ahs without the call to prayer or iqamah. He said: Then he addressed us and called upon God, and he turned his face towards the Qiblah, raising his hands. Then he turned his cloak over, placing the right hand over the left, and the left over the right.” Abu Bakr said: There is a lot of confusion in his hadith on the authority of Al-Zuhri, so if this news is proven then it is An indication of: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, delivered a sermon and called, and turned his robe twice: once before the prayer, and once after it.”"
